meta {
  name: SyncPoliciesFromHub
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{PROVIDER_MANAGEMENT}}/v1alpha/policyhub/policies/sync
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Re-imports every policy definition previously imported from the Construct-X Policy Hub right
  away - the same run the control plane otherwise performs periodically (every hour by default,
  see constructx.policyhub.sync.*). Only the connector's own imports (those carrying
  "privateProperties.policyHubName") are synced; hand-written policies are left
  alone. Runs synchronously, no body.

  Response: counts of "checked", "updated", "unchanged" and "failed" policy definitions. A policy
  is only written when its content in the hub changed. Failed policies (e.g. hub returns 404 or
  the new version fails validation) are kept unchanged - the control plane log shows the reason as
  a warning ("Policy Hub sync (manual): keeping policy definition ... unchanged: ...").

  If the Policy Hub itself is unreachable (connection refused, timeout, 5xx, 408, 429), this
  request does not wait for it: it aborts right away with 503 Service Unavailable, and the log
  shows "Policy Hub sync (manual) aborted: Policy Hub unreachable (...)". Only the periodic sync
  waits for the hub (up to 60 s) and, if it stays away, retries the run every 5 minutes. To try
  it: docker stop policyhub-backend, run this request, then docker start policyhub-backend.

  If the Policy Hub rejects the connector's credentials (401/403, e.g. a wrong secret under the
  vault alias policy-hub-credentials), the run aborts at once without waiting and this request
  answers 502 Bad Gateway; the log shows "Policy Hub sync (manual) aborted: Policy Hub rejected
  the credentials (...)". The periodic sync aborts the same way and tries again after 5 minutes,
  so a corrected secret takes effect without a restart.

  To try it: run ImportPolicyFromHub, change the policy in the Policy Hub, run this request and
  check with Check Imported Policy that the new version and
  "privateProperties.policyHubImportedAt" are there.

  Prerequisite: the Policy Hub stack (policy-hub/docker-compose.yml) is running on port 8080.
}
